OL,3,AWill a switch to light speed cut power
OL,4,Ause at data centres?
OL,5,
OL,6,F"I think we're at the end of copper,"
OL,7,Fsays Chris Sharp, the chief technology
OL,8,Fofficer at data centre operator Digital
OL,9,FRealty.
OL,11,FHe's not saying that we are running out
OL,12,Fof copper, instead Sharp, and many
OL,13,Fothers in the data centre industry, are
OL,14,Fbetting that it will be used less.
OL,16,FData centres use vast amounts of the
OL,17,Fmetal: around 400 tonnes will go into a
OL,18,Ftypical facility of around 100MW (data
OL,19,Fcentre size is measured megawatts, a
OL,20,Funit of electrical power).
OL,23,APub: 22-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,114,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11302
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F113A1790205856
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,AWill a switch to light speed cut power
OL,4,Ause at data centres?
OL,5,
OL,6,FMost of that copper is used in the
OL,7,Felectrical infrastructure needed to
OL,8,Fpower the datacentre and for cooling
OL,9,Fsystems. But up to 70 tonnes is used by
OL,10,Fthe computer servers that do the work
OL,11,Fof processing data in that 100MW
OL,12,Ffacility.
OL,23,APub: 22-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,114,105,200,160,0,100
